WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:00.333
And I

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.334
want to go to Ty Cobb now,

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.420
the former Trump White House lawyer.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.671
So, Ty, you know,

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.173
you hear what happened today

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.717
and the way Andrea described it

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:09.300
that Trump as

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.385
a spectator was sitting there.

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:11.094
No one could look at him.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.679
He couldn't do anything.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.555
He had to sit there all day

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:14.305
and listen to a lecture

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:15.682
on gap accounting,

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.851
all to get in front of that camera

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.893
for those few moments

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.812
when he came out and say,

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.230
well, I should be in Iowa

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.648
and now he's going to take the stand

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:26.860
on Monday, again, for the for the

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.528
this is now going to be again,

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.904
because he did testify last month.

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:32.115
It was nearly 4 hours

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.450
that he testified last time.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:33.992
At one point,

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:37.078
he said it is a terrible, terrible thing

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:37.620
you've done.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.121
You believe

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:39.539
this political hack back there

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.124
and that's unfortunate.

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:42.167
So now he goes back on

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.251
the stand on Monday.

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:46.254
How do you think this is going to go, Ty?

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:49.340
Well, first of all, Aaron, I would say

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:50.258
nice to be with you.

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:53.178
Thanks for having me on that.

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.637
I'm not sure you will testify.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:57.891
I'd say it's still 5050 because

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:01.978
as as the lawyer in me says,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.271
you know, why put him on?

00:01:03.271 --> 00:01:04.314
I mean, he's going to be subject

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:06.149
to an eviscerating cross-examination,

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.776
which won't focus on,

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.193
you know,

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:09.861
what, Trump wants to talk about it.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:12.739
Focus on every lie that he told,

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:13.073
you know,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.449
in the ten years

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:15.116
that are relevant

00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:17.368
under these financial statements.

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:19.829
And as we know, I mean, he told

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:20.955
several more whoppers

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.291
on the steps of the court today.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:25.752
There's a lot of material to work with.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.755
So I think a talented, skillful

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.298
prosecutor

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:32.342
could cross-examine him in a way

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.260
that would just eviscerate him.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.262
On the other hand, that's the legal

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.388
that's the legal side.

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:40.016
As you all were discussing correctly,

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:41.726
this really isn't legal anymore

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:43.853
because it's clear

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:46.147
that his assets were inflated.

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:46.856
It's clear

00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:47.899
that there are multiple

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.610
misstatements, misrepresentations

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.071
and lies on the on the numbers

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.572
that were provided.

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:56.157
And that's all the statute

00:01:56.157 --> 00:01:56.991
Statute doesn't

00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:58.576
talk about gap accounting.

00:01:58.576 --> 00:01:59.494
The statute doesn't

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:01.287
talk about materiality.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.290
The statute just says misrepresentations

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.333
and omissions,

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:07.877
even without a materiality standard.

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:08.586
So that's

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:09.838
that's why the judge was able

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:12.382
to rule in advance of trial

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:15.385
that Trump was Trump was guilty

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:19.514
of of fraud and and subject to penalties.

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:22.142
And this is this is really more about,

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.226
you know, the disgorgement,

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:25.603
the amount of money

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:27.689
that Trump will have will have to pay.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.692
So there's there is nothing

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:31.317
that Trump said

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.027
on the courthouse steps today.

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:33.987
You know, that's true.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.363
Other than, you know, I'm

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:36.239
I'm happy to be here

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:38.116
because he had a free microphone,

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:39.742
which you wouldn't have had in Iowa or

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.244
he wouldn't have had.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.120
Well, and then that makes

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.746
him look like everybody else

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:44.455
that's running. Right.

00:02:44.455 --> 00:02:45.456
Which he obviously doesn't want to do,

00:02:45.456 --> 00:02:46.541
because he could have been at the debate.

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:47.542
He could be in Iowa there.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:49.711
He purposely seems to avoid

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:50.753
where they are.

00:02:50.753 --> 00:02:51.629
But when you talk about how

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:52.630
this all comes down to what

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:53.882
the amount of disgorgement will be,

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:54.507
how much money

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.341
Trump will have to pay, and,

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.050
of course, whether

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.635
whether he'd be able to do business again

00:02:57.635 --> 00:02:59.429
in the way he defines it.

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:02.056
How significant how big do you think that

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:04.142
that number could be,

00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:06.394
given what you've seen thus far?

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:09.731
Well, she's asked for $250 million.

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:11.274
I think the evidence,

00:03:11.274 --> 00:03:11.566
you know,

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:13.651
the most compelling evidence on damages

00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:17.071
so far is that was the evidence that came

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:19.157
in that suggested that

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.451
the Trump Organization had saved

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.454
$168 million

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:26.998
or received a benefit of $168 million

00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:27.957
that would not have otherwise

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.960
been entitled to because of the

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.337
documents provided.

00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:34.839
So I think that's I think $168

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:36.424
million is in evidence.

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:38.843
I'm not sure what additional arguments

00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:41.721
will be made to enhance that figure.

00:03:41.804 --> 00:03:43.139
And then, you know, the

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:45.183
real risk is, of course, the

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:46.643
the possibility

00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:47.977
of losing the ability

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:49.979
to do business in New York,

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:50.730
which as

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.272
as we know,

00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:54.234
the Court of appeals today said,

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:54.734
you know,

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:55.735
they were going to reserve

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.153
decision on that

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:57.820
until

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.114
until they consider the entire appeal,

00:04:00.114 --> 00:04:02.492
which is which is the ordinary process.

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.410
And frankly, the way it should be done

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.954
is being treated by Trump courts

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:06.871
as a giant victory.

00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:08.623
But really, it's it's

00:04:08.623 --> 00:04:09.374
sort of the only way

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:10.917
the case could have proceeded.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.586
All right, Ty, thank you.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.921
My pleasure. Great to be with you.

